WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.269
[music playing]

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:28.428
JIM SHEDD: Gilberto Rogriuez
Orejuela and Miguel Rodriguez

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:31.131
Orejuela were the
heads of a cartel

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:34.834
that was totally different
than the other cartels.

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:40.140
They looked at it more
as a business to expand,

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:44.577
and they were involved in
the cost versus profit.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:55.355
You have to learn who your
enemy is, otherwise you're

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:56.423
not going to win the fight.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:03.530
And I , studied over
a long period of time,

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:06.966
the Rodriguez Orejuelas,
and they were very smart,

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.102
strategic thinkers
who were always

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:12.238
one step ahead of the game.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:14.140
NARRATOR: Gilberto
and Miguel Rodriguez

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.509
have a piece of
several hotels and own

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.445
Cali's largest shopping center.

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:27.754
NEWS ANNOUNCER: And they
own Cali's main passion,

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:29.355
the soccer team America.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:41.401
JIM SHEDD: So, they
were to be respected.

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:43.503
Yes, they were dopers
and traffickers, but you

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.004
cannot underestimate them.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:48.141
You underestimate people of
that caliber, you're doomed.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.014
WILLIAM RODRIGUEZ: My
name is William Rodriguez.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:58.885
I'm the son and nephew of the
Cali cartel founders, Miguel

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.753
and Gilberto Rodriguez Orejuela.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:07.660
There was a strategic
alliance between my dad,

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.528
my uncle, and Escobar.

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:15.201
They had different ways
to see how we should fight

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:17.270
this war against authorities.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:20.139
Escobar wanted to do
it through violence.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:23.142
We wanted to do
it by corruption.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:31.818
My dad Miguel was called
El Senor, the Sir.

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:35.221
My uncle Gilberto built
an economic empire.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.690
He wanted to fulfill
his dream with my dad,

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:40.260
because he wanted my
dad to be a lawyer.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.861
And that's why I
wanted to be a lawyer.

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:42.829
I want to be like my dad.

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.564
I wanted to help my family.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:50.270
People think that bandits
don't have values.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.738
But my dad and uncle did.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:52.939
They have honor.

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:55.208
Violence was the last step
to resolve the problems,

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:57.677
because dead people
don't pay what they owe.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.848
NARRATOR: Gilberto
Miguel Rodriquez

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:05.418
are forcing modern business
methods on a violent trade.

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:13.226
NARRATOR: The cartel forced
its employees to fill

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:15.495
out this application form.

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:18.865
Cartel hopefuls had to enter
the names and addresses

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.800
of their entire family.

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:22.702
JIM SHEDD: They had to know
who your family members were,

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:24.804
where were they, what
did they own, didn't own.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.373
Cars, planes, automobiles,
trains, anything.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.242
They had to know all
about you before you

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:30.677
were trusted into the system.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.782
WILLIAM RODRIGUEZ: The
moving of the cocaine,

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.417
they did it by different ways.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.986
First, they did it into little
planes into the Caribbean

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:42.221
and in Central America.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:45.592
Then they shifted in to
doing it through Mexico.

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:48.528
NARRATOR: To handle the ever
larger shipments of cocaine

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:51.230
heading to the United
States, the cartel

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:54.834
used container ships,
sometimes even loading

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.603
up entire passenger jets.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:06.879
NARRATOR: It is a
marriage of convenience

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:11.217
between Colombia's Cali
cartel and the Italian mafia.

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:14.988
When the Cold War
ended, a new war began.

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:16.489
NARRATOR: The problem
of cocaine in Russia

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:18.791
began only one or two years ago.

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:22.362
Cocaine is a new problem for us.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:31.571
NARRATOR: From Moscow to
Madrid, from Rome to Tokyo,

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:34.273
the Cali cartel is
creating new markets.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:42.749
NARRATOR: In raw
profit, it now outstrips

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:46.285
Boeing, Texaco, and Pepsi.

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:49.088
WILLIAM RODRIGUEZ: They had so
much power in those moments,

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:51.324
they thought they were
on the top of the world.

00:04:57.764 --> 00:05:01.100
JIM SHEDD: They were
planning to eventually become

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.435
the Kennedys of Colombia.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.372
WILLIAM RODRIGUEZ: In
the narcos cassettes,

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:10.610
you can see the power that
Miguel and Gilberto had,

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:12.879
because this guy is
saying you have the future

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.514
of Colombia in your hands.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:18.184
If you give this money,
you will have a President.

